```

## Randomized Encouragement Design Analysis

We model the following ordinary least squares 

$$Y_{it}=\alpha + \beta_1 Encouragement_{i} + X \gamma + W \beta_2 + \epsilon_{it}$$
Where:

- $Y_{it}$ represents electricity consumption (kWh) for consumer $i$ at the half-hour level $t$ during Saving Sessions or the logarithmic electricity consumption (excluding half-hours with 0kWh consumption) 
- $Encouragement_{i}$ is a binary variable: 1 if the customer i is part of the treatment group (received an email invitation encouraging sign-up to OctoPlus) and 0 if in the control group.
- $\beta_1$ represents the impact of being encouraged to sign up to OctoPlus
- $X$ is a vector of customer characteristics, including previous consumption (in the final version, we would use consumption prior to the first date of OctoPlus sign-up encouragement emails being sent out by Octopus Energy but in here we use Estimated Annual Consumption), is the customer prepay and GSP regions (variables we stratified on) 
- $W$ a set of weather controls averaged for the last 24h that varies at the regional level: heating degree days, wind speed, cloud coverage
- $\epsilon_{it}$ represents the error term. We cluster standard errors at the level of consumer $i$. 


